{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before your tool deletes a file, your tool must get a confirmation from the user. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestInput"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context"},{"type":"text","value":" for that confirmation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx"},{"type":"text","value":" is the second argument of the function you pass to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".server()"},{"type":"text","value":". Give "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".server()"},{"type":"text","value":" the type "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MCPToolContext"},{"type":"text","value":", so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.requestInput"},{"type":"text","value":" type-checks."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport type { MCPToolContext } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst deleteFile = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'delete_file',\n  description: 'Delete a file after the user says yes',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    path: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server<MCPToolContext>(async ({ path }, ctx) => {\n  const answer = await ctx.context.requestInput({\n    message: `Delete ${path}? Type yes to continue.`,\n  })\n\n  if (answer !== 'yes') {\n    return `Kept ${path}.`\n  }\n\n  return `Deleted ${path}.`\n})\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'files',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  tools: [deleteFile],\n})\n\nexport function fetch(request: Request) {\n  return server.fetch(request)\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestInput"},{"type":"text","value":" returns the string that the user sends."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the user declines or cancels, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestInput"},{"type":"text","value":" throws an Error. The tool call then ends with a tool error."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"spec-2025-and-spec-2026","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spec 2025 and spec 2026"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On spec 2025, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestInput"},{"type":"text","value":" needs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sessions: 'memory'"},{"type":"text","value":". It waits on the open session, and the same tool call then continues with the answer. Without a session, it throws. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./server-sessions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP Server Sessions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On spec 2026, the handler returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input_required"},{"type":"text","value":". Then the client runs the tool again with the answer. On spec 2026, the code before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestInput"},{"type":"text","value":" runs on each call, so it can run more than once."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the work must run once, put that work after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestInput"},{"type":"text","value":" returns."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On spec 2026, a tool asks one question per call. A second "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestInput"},{"type":"text","value":" in the same call throws an Error. To ask two questions, use two tools."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A TanStack "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" host pauses on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input_required"},{"type":"text","value":" and shows the request to the user. "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/mcp-input","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP Client Input"}]},{"type":"text","value":" shows how the user answers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestInput"},{"type":"text","value":" does not work in an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execution: 'task'"},{"type":"text","value":" tool. "},{"type":"link","href":"./server-tasks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP Server Tasks"}]},{"type":"text","value":" has the details."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the user sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"yes"},{"type":"text","value":", the tool returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Deleted"},{"type":"text","value":" plus the file path."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"spec-2025-and-spec-2026","text":"Spec 2025 and spec 2026","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nBefore your tool deletes a file, your tool must get a confirmation from the user. Call `requestInput` on `ctx.context` for that confirmation.\n\n`ctx` is the second argument of the function you pass to `.server()`. Give `.server()` the type `MCPToolContext`, so `ctx.context.requestInput` type-checks.\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport type { MCPToolContext } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst deleteFile = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'delete_file',\n  description: 'Delete a file after the user says yes',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    path: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server<MCPToolContext>(async ({ path }, ctx) => {\n  const answer = await ctx.context.requestInput({\n    message: `Delete ${path}? Type yes to continue.`,\n  })\n\n  if (answer !== 'yes') {\n    return `Kept ${path}.`\n  }\n\n  return `Deleted ${path}.`\n})\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'files',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  tools: [deleteFile],\n})\n\nexport function fetch(request: Request) {\n  return server.fetch(request)\n}\n```\n\n`requestInput` returns the string that the user sends.\n\nIf the user declines or cancels, `requestInput` throws an Error. The tool call then ends with a tool error.\n\n## Spec 2025 and spec 2026\n\nOn spec 2025, `requestInput` needs `sessions: 'memory'`. It waits on the open session, and the same tool call then continues with the answer. Without a session, it throws. See [MCP Server Sessions](./server-sessions).\n\nOn spec 2026, the handler returns `input_required`. Then the client runs the tool again with the answer. On spec 2026, the code before `requestInput` runs on each call, so it can run more than once.\n\nIf the work must run once, put that work after `requestInput` returns.\n\nOn spec 2026, a tool asks one question per call. A second `requestInput` in the same call throws an Error. To ask two questions, use two tools.\n\nA TanStack `chat()` host pauses on `input_required` and shows the request to the user. [MCP Client Input](../tools/mcp-input) shows how the user answers.\n\n`requestInput` does not work in an `execution: 'task'` tool. [MCP Server Tasks](./server-tasks) has the details.\n\nIf the user sends `yes`, the tool returns `Deleted` plus the file path.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Ask for Input\nid: mcp-server-input\norder: 13\ndescription: \"Ask the user for a value inside an MCP server tool with requestInput.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - mcp\n  - model context protocol\n  - requestInput\n  - confirmation\n  - input required\n  - MCPToolContext\n---\n\nBefore your tool deletes a file, your tool must get a confirmation from the user. Call `requestInput` on `ctx.context` for that confirmation.\n\n`ctx` is the second argument of the function you pass to `.server()`. Give `.server()` the type `MCPToolContext`, so `ctx.context.requestInput` type-checks.\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport type { MCPToolContext } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst deleteFile = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'delete_file',\n  description: 'Delete a file after the user says yes',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    path: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server<MCPToolContext>(async ({ path }, ctx) => {\n  const answer = await ctx.context.requestInput({\n    message: `Delete ${path}? Type yes to continue.`,\n  })\n\n  if (answer !== 'yes') {\n    return `Kept ${path}.`\n  }\n\n  return `Deleted ${path}.`\n})\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'files',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  tools: [deleteFile],\n})\n\nexport function fetch(request: Request) {\n  return server.fetch(request)\n}\n```\n\n`requestInput` returns the string that the user sends.\n\nIf the user declines or cancels, `requestInput` throws an Error. The tool call then ends with a tool error.\n\n## Spec 2025 and spec 2026\n\nOn spec 2025, `requestInput` needs `sessions: 'memory'`. It waits on the open session, and the same tool call then continues with the answer. Without a session, it throws. See [MCP Server Sessions](./server-sessions).\n\nOn spec 2026, the handler returns `input_required`. Then the client runs the tool again with the answer. On spec 2026, the code before `requestInput` runs on each call, so it can run more than once.\n\nIf the work must run once, put that work after `requestInput` returns.\n\nOn spec 2026, a tool asks one question per call. A second `requestInput` in the same call throws an Error. To ask two questions, use two tools.\n\nA TanStack `chat()` host pauses on `input_required` and shows the request to the user. [MCP Client Input](../tools/mcp-input) shows how the user answers.\n\n`requestInput` does not work in an `execution: 'task'` tool. [MCP Server Tasks](./server-tasks) has the details.\n\nIf the user sends `yes`, the tool returns `Deleted` plus the file path.\n"}
